+# Blind full-portfolio ideation — round 20260831T1033Z
+
+## 1. Disposition vector
+
+“Unchanged” retains the frozen inventory *and* its live overlays; it does not revive a row already marked dead, retired, or stopped. The baseline is the 46-row table [A:184–235].
+
+| # | Avenue (short name) | Disposition | Reason for change |
+|---:|---|---|---|
+| 1 | GGV corner families / farm | unchanged | — |
+| 2 | Sheet ladder / dicritical trees | **raise** | Its colouring subroute is saturated and must stop, but the typed dicritical-budget subroute has just produced the rank-four irreducibility theorem and has an all-degree successor [R4:19–44; W:27–31]. |
+| 3 | Strip ODE / residue functional | unchanged | — |
+| 4 | Formal germs / algebraization | unchanged | — |
+| 5 | Jung–van der Kulk descent | unchanged | — |
+| 6 | Abhyankar–Moh / one-place recognition | **reopen** | The earlier category error was applying one-place theory to multi-place fibres; rank four now supplies the correct object: one irreducible, `A1`-normalized, one-place component of `A_F` [R4:28–35, 46–55]. Reopening is only for its semigroup/attainment content, not for the old fibre argument. |
+| 7 | Nonproperness / `A(F)` | **raise** | At rank four `A_F` is no longer an unpinned reducible collection: the charged branch is one component, making realization tests materially sharper [R4:12–15, 46–55]. |
+| 8 | Formal inverse combinatorics | unchanged | — |
+| 9 | Lee–Li / Magnus remainder | unchanged | — |
+| 10 | HC4 bridge | unchanged | — |
+| 11 | Mathieu / GMC / Poisson ladder | unchanged | — |
+| 12 | Face isolation / p-adic multinomials | unchanged | — |
+| 13 | Dixmier `DC(2)` | unchanged | — |
+| 14 | `End(A1)` disproof audit | unchanged | — |
+| 15 | Spectral surfaces / commuting PDOs | unchanged | — |
+| 16 | D-module / holonomic index | unchanged | — |
+| 17 | BCW–Drużkowski stabilization | unchanged | — |
+| 18 | Graded / equivariant / GIT | unchanged | — |
+| 19 | Characteristic-​`p` + Witt lifting | **raise** | It now has a first exact bounded frontier—correction `y`-degree 12—whereas another unrestricted Witt level is known to be uninformative [A:208]. This is the cleanest falsification-side finite question. |
+| 20 | Reduction mod `p` / p-curvature | unchanged | — |
+| 21 | p-adic injectivity / Hensel | **raise** | Coupling the 109-sheet Hensel decomposition to the same degree-12 support frontier gives a second observable (`A_infinity`) rather than another completion-only argument [A:210]. |
+| 22 | Integral points / heights | unchanged | — |
+| 23 | Analytic global inverse / metric | unchanged | — |
+| 24 | Real JC / Pinchuk | unchanged | — |
+| 25 | Fibre monodromy / passports | **raise** | Passports alone remain exhausted, but the promoted irreducible branch and source-cover data permit a permutation-local-system/Alexander receiver, described in §4; this is genuinely coupled information, not a 170th passport [A:214, 276]. |
+| 26 | Primitive monodromy / Galois | **raise** | The reviewed `N-1` budget suggests a typed all-degree component bound, while the all-degree nontrivial-`pi1` theorem supplies a distinguished component [P:24–39; R4:19–44]. |
+| 27 | Links / splice / plumbing | **raise** | The one-node meridional theorem is now promoted at every degree, and the remaining target is precisely unibranch/tangential attainment rather than another raw splice census [H:69–96; A:130–138]. |
+| 28 | Log surfaces / BMY / boundary models | **raise** | One explicit SNC model now returns the decisive integer `Theta_h`; the old “needs data” row has acquired a named, minimal datum [A:23–28; R4:73–90]. |
+| 29 | LND / Hamiltonian completeness | **lower** | On the exact one-cusp ring both hypothetical coordinate flows are proved non-locally-finite with hyperbolic generic fibres; LND, `A1`, `C*`, Picard, ML and ruling shortcuts must not be rerun [H:49–67; A:88–94]. The wild valuation successor is retained under rows 2/28. |
+| 30 | Affine-surface classification / ML | unchanged | — |
+| 31 | Integrality / ZMT / Rees | unchanged | — |
+| 32 | Off-diagonal collision ideal | unchanged | — |
+| 33 | Symplectic exactness / residues | unchanged | — |
+| 34 | 2D tangent sweep / pole removal | unchanged | — |
+| 35 | Higher-dimensional descent | unchanged | — |
+| 36 | Guided sparse counterexample search | unchanged | — |
+| 37 | Finite-field census | unchanged | — |
+| 38 | Tropical coefficient geometry | unchanged | — |
+| 39 | Cohomological cluster | unchanged | — |
+| 40 | Free-associative lift | unchanged | — |
+| 41 | Naive scaling deformation | unchanged | — |
