+| 45 | Differential Galois | unchanged | — |
+| 46 | Formal certification / AI | unchanged | — |
+
+## 2. Bottleneck reranking
+
+### Proof bottlenecks
+
+1. **Universal landing plus a cofinal generic-degree bound.** No collection of rank-four or other bounded-class exclusions proves JC2 until arbitrary Keller maps land faithfully in the charged architecture and the “always a next degree” escape is closed [A:171–172, 190–191].
+2. **All-degree typing of the dicritical budget.** The proof `2m <= N-1` is reviewed only in the plane degree-four canonical setting, and the integration expressly forbids exporting Orevkov names beyond that scope without rebuilding the hypotheses [R4:19–47].
+3. **Algebraic attainment of surviving one-place data.** Colourability is only a necessary condition, and explicit survivors at `Delta_aff=6,7,9,10,12,13,15,...` leave the actual charged-curve realization problem untouched [A:12–22; W:20–31].
+4. **One concrete SNC boundary model for the one-cusp horn.** All abstract identities needed for the four-row partition are promoted, but neither `d_h` nor `r_h` exists as campaign data until one charged coordinate is resolved [R4:73–90].
+5. **Topology beyond the clean one-node case.** The promoted meridional obstruction says nothing about tangencies, unibranch affine conductors, additional singularities, nonsimple inertia, or disconnected covers [H:91–96].
+
+### Disproof bottlenecks
+
+1. **Uniform polynomial complexity.** The AS seed lifts through every Witt level only by growing support/degree and converges to a nonpolynomial restricted-analytic object, so a counterexample needs one support bound surviving all levels [A:175, 208].
+2. **Formal-germ algebraization with route provenance.** Modular nonemptiness, compatible jets, a characteristic-zero formal germ, and a polynomial Keller map are four distinct stages; K00 remains stuck at the last two and can also lose its source route during gluing [A:193].
+3. **Global nonproperness/collision, not merely `J=1`.** A finite-support lift or sparse solution is useful only if it also carries a certified off-diagonal collision or equivalent global nonproperness datum; otherwise it can simply be an automorphism.
+4. **A source-complete search grammar above the classical firewalls.** Below the known bounds the region is already empty, while above them generic sparse supports overwhelmingly miss the thin Keller locus [A:225, 278].
+
+## 3. New avenue or mechanism
+
+### Floer correction terms as an **attainment** sieve
+
+For a surviving rank-four candidate, homogenize the proposed irreducible `A1`-normalized one-place curve to `\bar B subset CP^2`. When every singularity of `\bar B` is unibranch, the candidate is a rational cuspidal plane curve; its projective degree and local value semigroups must satisfy the Heegaard–Floer correction-term inequalities of Borodzik–Livingston and their arbitrary-genus extension. These are effective inequalities on semigroup-counting functions, so the delta-sequence compiler can test them by integer arithmetic. The primary sources are Borodzik–Livingston, *Heegaard Floer homology and rational cuspidal curves*, Forum Math. Sigma 2 (2014), e28, [arXiv:1304.1062](https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.1062), and Borodzik–Hedden–Livingston, *Plane algebraic curves of arbitrary genus via Heegaard Floer homology*, Comment. Math. Helv. 92 (2017), 215–256, [doi:10.4171/CMH/411](https://doi.org/10.4171/CMH/411).
+
+This is genuinely different from Avenue 27's splice colourings: a colourable knot can still fail the smooth four-manifold correction-term constraints required of an algebraic plane-curve realization. It directly targets the new live gap—attainment of the explicit survivors [A:12–22, 41–48]—and never upgrades a passing necessary-condition test to existence.
+
+For noncuspidal controls, Borodzik–Liu–Zemke construct link-Floer/knotification obstructions and explicitly treat transverse double points in *Heegaard Floer homology, knotifications of links, and plane curves with noncuspidal singularities*, Algebr. Geom. Topol. 24 (2024), 4837–4889, [doi:10.2140/agt.2024.24.4837](https://doi.org/10.2140/agt.2024.24.4837). That paper licenses a node branch of the compiler and a regression against the promoted one-node kill; it does **not** by itself license arbitrary tangencies. A tangential or general multibranch record therefore returns typed `OPEN` until its exact link-cobordism hypotheses are proved.
+
+## 4. New connection between existing avenues
+
+### A Shapiro–twisted-Alexander receiver for monodromy
+
+Connect Avenues 7, 25–27 and the source-incidence data as follows. Put `U=C^2\B` and, only after checking that this is the actual finite étale locus, `V=C^2\F^{-1}(B)`. The degree-`N` monodromy gives a permutation local system `C^N = 1 + V_std` on `U`. Shapiro's lemma identifies homology with coefficients in `C^N` with ordinary homology of `V`; hence the standard summand measures the difference between source-complement and target-complement homology. The number and incidence of irreducible components of `F^{-1}(B)` can therefore provide a *lower* constraint, while the singular links of `B` provide an *upper/divisibility* constraint.
+
+The latter is not a slogan: for a unitary representation, Cogolludo Agustín–Florens prove that the twisted Alexander polynomial of a plane-curve complement divides the product of the local twisted polynomials, with the quotient controlled by a Blanchfield form; see *Twisted Alexander polynomials of plane algebraic curves*, J. Lond. Math. Soc. 76 (2007), 105–121, [doi:10.1112/jlms/jdm004](https://doi.org/10.1112/jlms/jdm004), [arXiv:math/0504356](https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0504356). A finite permutation representation is unitarizable. Thus a candidate `S4` colouring can be tested against source-cover homology, not merely against a Hurwitz identity tuple. Before promotion one must separately prove the affine/projective-at-infinity convention, torsion hypothesis, and exact linking map; if any is missing the result is `OPEN`, not a vanishing claim.
+
+A second connection is immediate but presently conditional: if the degree-four dicritical proof types at general `N`, then the distinct-per-component charges give `2m <= N-1`; pairing this with the promoted theorem that at least one branch component has nontrivial `pi1` turns the all-degree topology lane into a bounded-component classification rather than an unrestricted curve-complement problem [P:24–39; R4:19–44].
+
+## 5. Strongest attacks available this week
+
+### Proof attack
+
+**Build exactly one charged one-cusp SNC boundary model and extract `Theta_h`.** The completion, boundary valuations, fibre connectedness and partition identity are already promoted; the missing object is geometric, not another formal manipulation [R4:73–90]. The cheapest decisive computation is a hand-checkable divisor table for the horizontal component `h`, recording the definitions of `d_h` and `r_h`, their intersection/valuation derivation, and then the single subtraction `Theta_h=d_h-r_h-2`. Negative or odd kills the configuration; nonnegative even selects a partition row and nothing more—especially not attainment [A:23–28]. Use no pole identity until the vertex class and every source hypothesis are checked.
+
+### Counterexample / falsification attack
+
+**Test the canonical fixed-support AS109 correction at maximum `y`-degree 12.** This is the first bounded frontier not already excluded [A:208–210]. Freeze the support, coefficient field, gauge, generator order, collision pair and reduction map; at the first unsolved Witt step form the linearized determinant-one equations together with the lifted-collision equations and compute an exact sparse rank certificate over `F_109`. No solution kills that declared support cell and raises the bounded lower frontier; a solution merely advances the same frozen support to the next Witt level. It does not turn the known growing-support tower or its restricted-analytic limit into a polynomial map. Start with a desk-scale matrix-shape/rank estimate; if dimensions or fill-in are uncertain, execute only on AWS as required by [P:29–33].
+
+## 6. Software acceleration or decisive experiment
+
+Implement a small, exact `attainment_sieve` (ordinary integer arithmetic, no CAS). Its typed input is `(projective_degree, normalization_genus, singularity_records[])`; each singularity record declares `UNIBRANCH_SEMIGROUP`, `TRANSVERSE_NODE`, or `UNLICENSED_MULTIBRANCH`, and the infinity record additionally carries the reduced delta-sequence and the declared semigroup map. The program should:
+
+1. verify the genus formula and semigroup conductors;
+2. compute the infimal-convolution/semigroup-counting functions required by the cited Floer theorem;
+3. emit the first violated inequality with all counts as a replay certificate, or `PASS_NECESSARY_ONLY`;
+4. return `OPEN` on a tangency or missing projective degree instead of guessing a semigroup.
+
+Controls: a named realizable rational cuspidal curve must pass; a hand-mutated count must fail; the promoted clean one-node class should be routed through the 2024 noncuspidal branch as a regression; an unlicensed tangency must return `OPEN`. The first production input is the smallest colourable `Delta_aff=6` survivor [A:18–22]. This experiment is cheap enough for the desk and, unlike extending the conductor census, can kill an attained-looking row for a new reason.
